Skip source-checkout-only CLI install and teleop tests on installed packages.

Several cli/ unit tests load the repository root pyproject.toml or run a
script from the source scripts/ directory, so they only work from a source
checkout and fail against an installed package:

  - test_install_command_parsing.py: TestCommandInstallDispatch drives
    command_install(), which loads the root pyproject even with the dependency
    installers mocked.
  - test_install.py: TestEnsureNewton.test_installs_pinned_release_when_absent
    calls install._load_root_pyproject().
  - test_install_commands.py: the two TestInstallRootExtraExcludesIsaacSim
    tests read the teleop extra from the root pyproject.
  - test_teleop_entrypoints.py: test_teleop_workflow_help_exposes_task_preset_selectors
    executes scripts/.../*.py from ISAACLAB_ROOT.

Gate them the same way the rest of the source-checkout-only suite is gated,
by requesting the source_checkout_root fixture, which skips when there is no
source checkout. The teleop help test also resolves its script from the
checkout root instead of ISAACLAB_ROOT, matching its sibling dispatch test.

